## Status

Self-excluded: **no verified public benchmark numbers** were found for the exact model/ID `gpt-5.4-mini` / `openai/gpt-5.4-mini` in accessible sources at time of research.

## Research notes

- Accessible metadata (not benchmark scores): Artificial Analysis lists GPT-5.4 mini (Xhigh) as a proprietary OpenAI reasoning model (released March 2026, deprecated in AA view), supporting text/image input and text output, with 400k-token context window, knowledge cutoff Aug 31 2025, and pricing around $0.75/$4.50 per 1M tokens (cache discount 90%) in AA snapshots. OpenRouter lists `openai/gpt-5.4-mini` with provider routing and supported parameters.
- OpenAI's "Introducing GPT-5.4" announcement reports benchmark results for GPT-5.4 / GPT-5.4 Pro variants; verifiable benchmark numbers explicitly and separately attributable to the exact `GPT-5.4 mini` model/ID were not found in accessible sources reviewed here.
- Artificial Analysis reported Intelligence Index and task-level benchmark aggregates as unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot; no standalone verified benchmark scores clearly attributable to this exact model/ID were found in accessible sources.
- Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`: if zero verified public benchmark numbers are found for the exact model/ID, save a notes-only `.md.excluded` file and do not invent placeholder scores.

